From c8cd2b58d01a4d5e2291167e66cfbc3bedc0822a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:24:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 102/104] docs: /v1/classify names executorch, and regenerate
 the API reference

The /v1/classify route spec listed onnxruntime and tflite text classifiers
only; it now names executorch too, as the label reference does. The
regenerated reference also carries the new 502
image_classification_unsupported on /v1/images/classify.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
---
 docs/api/lemonade.md                                  | 3 ++-
 src/cpp/server/routes/lemonade/inference/classify.cpp | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/api/lemonade.md b/docs/api/lemonade.md
index 0257bda62..c240120dd 100644
--- a/docs/api/lemonade.md
+++ b/docs/api/lemonade.md
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ Some Lemonade endpoints live on other pages: the per-model [`/v1/models/{id}/fil
 ## `POST /v1/classify`
 <sub>![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-experimental-orange)</sub>
 
-Runs an encoder text classifier, such as a PII, prompt-safety or domain classifier, on a string and returns a score for each label. It serves `onnxruntime` sequence classifiers (one label set), token classifiers (aggregated span labels) and zero-shot models (labels sent with each request), and `tflite` text classifiers; image models are served by [`POST /v1/images/classify`](#post-v1imagesclassify). It provides the classification that the router's `classifier` and `zero_shot` conditions use.
+Runs an encoder text classifier, such as a PII, prompt-safety or domain classifier, on a string and returns a score for each label. It serves `onnxruntime` sequence classifiers (one label set), token classifiers (aggregated span labels) and zero-shot models (labels sent with each request), and `tflite` and `executorch` text classifiers; image models are served by [`POST /v1/images/classify`](#post-v1imagesclassify). It provides the classification that the router's `classifier` and `zero_shot` conditions use.
 
 Requires `LEMONADE_API_KEY` when it is set.
 
@@ -258,6 +258,7 @@ An image model directory holds the graph (`model.tflite` for `tflite`, `model.pt
 | `500` |  | The request fails unexpectedly |
 | `500` | `model_load_error` | Loading the requested model fails for another reason, such as a failed download or a backend that does not start |
 | `502` | `backend_crashed_on_input` | The backend crashed on this input; the request is not retried, and the next request restarts the backend |
+| `502` | `image_classification_unsupported` | The engine answered 404 for its image route: it predates image classification (tflite-server 0.2.0, et-server 0.2.0 and ort-server 0.2.0-musl are the first releases that serve it) |
 | `503` | `server_busy` | Two image-classification requests are already in progress (`Retry-After: 1`) |
 | `503` | `backend_crash_cooldown` | The model's backend crashed on 3 inputs within 60 seconds, which pauses classification for that model for 60 seconds (with `Retry-After`) |
 | `504` | `backend_unresponsive_on_input` | The backend stopped answering its health checks while working on this input and was stopped; the request is not retried and does not count toward the crash pause |
